course: dictionary
lesson: 15785
title: Ultimately
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Ultimately» tells you what happens in the end, after everything else. «We practised every day for months, and ultimately the team won the cup.» The clue is «for months»: the hard work came first, and the win came last.
explain: The word can also mean the most important thing, the basic point under everything else. «The coach said, "Ultimately, it is your choice."» The coach is saying that the most important thing is what you decide.
explain: You may also meet «ultimately» in maths word problems. «Add the costs, take off the discount, and ultimately you have the price to pay.» Here it means at the end of all the steps. Look at the steps before it and you will spot the meaning.
fact: Ultimately means in the end, finally, after everything else.
fact: Ultimately can also mean at the most basic level, most importantly.
fact: «Ultimately, it is your choice» means the most important thing is that you decide.
fact: Ultimately is often used in stories, essays and exam answers to sum up the result or the main point.
fact: To check a meaning, swap in «in the end» or «after all» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «After many tries, ultimately she passed the test.» What does ultimately mean here? | At the start | Never | Very quickly | *In the end
exercise: «Ultimately, it is your choice.» What is the most important idea in this sentence? | Choices are always wrong | Someone else must decide for you | *The choice is yours and matters most | The weather is cold
exercise: «Add the numbers, share the total, and ultimately you get the answer.» Which phrase means about the same as ultimately here? | At the very beginning | Half way through | Without any steps at all | *At the end of all the steps
test: «The rain fell all week, but ultimately the sun came out on Saturday.» Ultimately means? | At the start of the week | *In the end | Very loudly | Hardly ever
test: Which sentence uses ultimately to mean most importantly? | We went swimming twice | The shop was closed on Monday | *Ultimately, friends are the people who care about you | The cat slept all day
exam: «Ben tried every route, got lost, asked for help, and ultimately found the way home.» What does ultimately tell us? | *The end result, after everything else | Rain on the way | A map of the town | The start of the trip
